            {
              "id": "7e66ce4f-771a-49d6-830d-661fac73ddf6",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": "<em><strong>God, Nimrod, &amp; the World: Exploring Christian Perspectives on Sport Hunting</strong></em> was written by Bracy V. Hill II &amp; John B. White, published by Mercer University Press, November 1, 2017."
            },
            {
              "id": "a4f806ac-fb9d-4d6b-9ed2-910a57e50acc",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "39b325fa-a460-4c8e-b41d-160095ca6141",
              "type": "quote",
              "html": "GOD, NIMROD, &amp; THE WORLD<em> presents the perspectives of more than two-dozen authors on the controversial sport of </em><a href=\"#/hunting\"><em>hunting</em></a><em>, surveying the relationship between the </em><a href=\"#/blood-sport\"><em>blood sport</em></a><em> and the salvation religion of Christianity.<br><br>The first half of the book provides sketches of the diverse interpretations of hunting in Hebrew and Christian cultures of the last two millennia, finally giving voice to those in the field who are both practitioners and persons of faith.<br><br>The second half offers prescriptions for the place of hunting in the life of contemporary Christians, with perspectives arguing for prohibition to those contending that hunting has a practical, even perfecting, place in the life of faith. The contributors, who hail from North America and the United Kingdom, include biblical scholars, theologians, philosophers, ethicists, historians, and sociologists, as well as professional athletes, celebrity hunters, teachers, musicians, healthcare professionals, and a soldier.</em>"
            },
            {
              "id": "089a9966-443c-4e9c-b797-3212189e48c5",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "html": ""
            }
